Located src/tags.ts via explore_project, then read it directly:

  export function normalizeTag(value: string): string {
    return value.toLowerCase();
  }

Only operation performed on `value` is toLowerCase() -- no trim, no replace, nothing that would strip leading or trailing whitespace before or after the case change. A caller passing "  Foo  " would get back "  foo  ", whitespace intact.

ANSWER: no
